# Accepted residual CVEs. Every entry documents why it is accepted and when to
# remove it. The Trivy gate in the release flow must pass with ONLY these
# suppressions -- a new finding means a new decision, not a new entry by reflex.
#
# SCOPE LIMITATION: trivy's ignorefile matches CVE IDs globally, with no
# per-image scoping -- the per-image section labels below are documentation,
# not enforcement. An entry accepted for one image also suppresses that CVE in
# the other two scans. Latent masks to watch: the mesa/glib render entries
# would also hide those CVEs if the GL tree ever re-enters the app image, and
# the starlette entries would hide a real finding if the app's starlette ever
# resolves below its fixed version (1.3.1 today). If either happens, split
# this into per-image ignore files passed via --ignorefile.

# -- Debian trixie base (python:*-slim): no fixed package released yet.
# Remove each when `apt-get upgrade` in a rebuild clears it from the scan.

# perl / perl-base / libperl5.40 / perl-modules-5.40 (CRITICAL x2, HIGH x3):
# interpreter ships in the slim base; nothing in Audicle invokes perl.
# Statuses: CVE-2026-8376 and CVE-2026-48962 are "affected"; the other three
# are "fix_deferred". All five are equally not-yet-fixed in trixie.
CVE-2026-42496
CVE-2026-42497
CVE-2026-8376
CVE-2026-48962
CVE-2026-9538

# curl / libcurl4t64 / libcurl3t64-gnutls (HIGH x10):
# system curl ships in base; backend Python httpx does not use system libcurl.
CVE-2026-12064
CVE-2026-5773
CVE-2026-6276
CVE-2026-8286
CVE-2026-8927
CVE-2026-8932
CVE-2026-9079
CVE-2026-9080
CVE-2026-9545
CVE-2026-9547

# libexpat1 (HIGH x6): XML parser in base; Audicle does not parse untrusted XML.
CVE-2025-59375
CVE-2026-25210
CVE-2026-45186
CVE-2026-56131
CVE-2026-56407
CVE-2026-56408

# ncurses (libncursesw6, libtinfo6, ncurses-base, ncurses-bin) (HIGH x1):
# terminal handling in base; Audicle runs headless in a container.
CVE-2025-69720

# gzip (HIGH x1): compression utility in base; not invoked by application code.
CVE-2026-41992

# libsndfile1 (HIGH x1): audio file library in the Debian base;
# Audicle uses soundfile (Python binding) for read/write only, no untrusted files.
CVE-2026-37555

# util-linux family (bsdutils, libblkid1, liblastlog2-2, libmount1, libsmartcols1,
# libuuid1, login, mount, util-linux) (HIGH x1):
# standard system utilities in the slim base; not exposed to untrusted input.
CVE-2026-53615

# libacl1 (HIGH x1): POSIX ACL library in base; no ACL operations in Audicle.
CVE-2026-54369

# -- render image only (python:3.12-slim + xvfb + mesa for Camoufox browser):

# xserver-common / xvfb (HIGH x3): Xvfb is required by Camoufox (headful browser
# in a virtual display). CVE-2023-5574 fix_deferred; 2026-55999/56000 affected.
# Remove when Debian ships a fix or the render image drops Xvfb.
CVE-2023-5574
CVE-2026-55999
CVE-2026-56000

# libxfont2 (HIGH x3): X font library pulled in by xvfb; no direct Audicle use.
# Remove when Debian ships fixes.
CVE-2026-56001
CVE-2026-56002
CVE-2026-56003

# mesa / libgbm1 / libgl1-mesa-dri / libglx-mesa0 / mesa-libgallium (CRITICAL x1
# will_not_fix): GPU/display drivers pulled in by Camoufox browser dependencies.
# Upstream will not fix; render container has no GPU access and no network exposure
# beyond the internal Docker network. Remove if mesa ships a fix or render drops GL.
CVE-2026-40393

# libglib2.0-0t64 (CRITICAL x1, HIGH x6): GLib pulled in by mesa/Camoufox deps.
# No fix released. Remove when Debian trixie ships a patched glib package.
CVE-2026-58010
CVE-2026-58011
CVE-2026-58012
CVE-2026-58013
CVE-2026-58014
CVE-2026-58015
CVE-2026-58016

# libtiff6 (HIGH x1): TIFF library pulled in by the render image's browser/mesa
# dependency chain. No fix released. Remove when Debian ships a patched libtiff6.
CVE-2026-12912

# libcups2t64 (HIGH x1): CUPS printing library in the render image (browser dep).
# No fix released. Remove when Debian ships a patch.
CVE-2026-34980

